+`--expert-substitute 0.15`: **1.29 → 2.77 tok/s = +115%**, at quality-neutral cost on
+both gates (tinyMMLU 66.0 → 67.0%, HumanEval pass@1 43/50 → 43/50). All mechanisms are
+**bmoe-main's** — it is the engine's headline, not the fork's. (2) fork vs bmoe-main —
+session/turn latency, not decode: divergence-turn prefill **2.2× faster** (42.6 → 19.3 s),
+follow-up prefill **~4× lower** (42 → 10–12 s), warmup+rs-seq composition putting T1 at
+2.6 s; the fork's decode contribution on this model is 0% by design. (The gate harness's
+warm-session 0.96 → 2.49 tok/s is substitution's warm-regime win, a bmoe-main mechanism.)
