+### Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (`qwen35moe` hybrid, 22.1 GB, ~2× host RAM)
+
+The largest model measured, the matrix's deepest thrash, and its first honest rewind
+refusal. Also the compute-bound cell where MTP pays (+29%), and the io-two-wave cell.
+
+**Recommended recipe (single-shot / cold sessions):**
+
+```bash
+bmoe-cli -m Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf \
+  --moe-stream --cache-mb auto --io-threads 4 --overlap --dense-weights anon \
+  --io-two-wave --release-mmap
+```
+
+**Add for served / multi-turn sessions:** warmup replay + `--auto-echo` — with a
+template check first: on this model the echo rewrite ENGAGED but never reconciled
+(`n_reused` 0 at every turn; prompts ballooned 52 → 185 → 350), so echo costs prefill and
+buys nothing until the template renders echoed reasoning the way the rewrite produces it.
+`--rs-seq 64` still buys the warmup composition (T1 2.6 s vs 13.2 s full-clear), but the
+divergence rewind REFUSED (depth 135 > 64 planes): a heavy thinker's single turn can
+outrun any affordable snapshot budget — the documented worst case, observed live.
+
+<details>
+<summary><strong>Per-flag table (provenance marked) — click to expand</strong></summary>
+
+| Flag | Provenance | Measured on this model | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| streaming stack (a→b) | **bmoe-main** | **+43%** (1.43 → 2.05 tok/s), majflt/tok **533 → 3.7** (~145× collapse, the deepest in the matrix), prefill 1.7× faster | **On** — the base for past-RAM models |
+| `--io-two-wave` | **bmoe-main** | **+25.2%** (1.763 → 2.208 tok/s, 256-tok regime), hard faults 5.1× lower (175.3 → 34.6/tok) | **Use-when**: past-RAM/thrash |
+| `--release-mmap` | **bmoe-main** | **+5.2%** (1.916 → 2.015, 256-tok regime), majflt/tok 50 → **0.83** (60×), decode reads −24%, load 7 s faster | **Use-when**: past-RAM/thrash |
+| `--mtp --draft 3` | **bmoe-main** (mainline concept) | **+29% clean** (Qwen3.6-MXFP4, DRAM-bound host cell; +15.1% under the drop recipe) — the compute-bound profile where speculation pays | **Use-when**: compute/DRAM-bound |
+| `--expert-substitute 0.15` | **bmoe-main** | quality-gated on this model, neutral (tinyMMLU 66.0 → 67.0% off→on vs stock, HumanEval pass@1 43/50 → 43/50 — per the substitution doc's device-protocol gate); the bench-cell A/B on Cyber-Tiel is the host speed number (+47.2%) | **Use-when**: thrash — quality-gated, neutral |
+| `--ubatch 512` | **mainline** | protocol default | **On** (protocol) |
+| `--ngram` | **mainline** (ngram-mod, upstream PR #19164) | not measured here on host | workload-dependent |
+| `--rs-seq 64` | **fork** (seam PR #29085) | T1 composes (2 prompt / 22 reused, 2.6 s vs 13.2 s); divergence rewind **REFUSED** (depth 135 > 64) — full clear, honest refusal costs ~6 s | **On** for served use (warmup composition); rewind budget-bounded |
+| warmup + `--auto-echo` (bridge) | **fork** (serve bridge) | warmup T1 17.9 → 13.2 s (cold-start only); echo ENGAGED, reuse 0 — never reconciled on this template | warmup **On**; echo **off here** until the template reconciles |
+| `--prefetch 1` · `--predict-prefetch` | **bmoe-main**, refuted | −24% (1.916 → 1.456, faults 50 → 245/tok) / −16% retention-only (1.612, faults 14.8/tok but observer tax) | **Keep-off** |
+
+</details>
+
+**Totals (two metrics).** (1) bmoe vs llama: baseline 1.43 → **2.05 tok/s (+43%)**,
+faults 533 → 3.7 (~145×), prefill 1.7× faster; the deepest-thrash cell also carries the
+biggest relative fault collapse — all bmoe-main. (2) fork vs bmoe-main: warmup+snapshot
+T1 composition (13.2 → 2.6 s) is real; the divergence rewind refuses at depth 135 and the
+echo rewrite never reconciles on this template — the two honest limits of the session
+layer, both documented. Decode contribution 0% by design.
+
+### Qwen3-30B-A3B (`qwen3moe` plain MoE, 18.6 GB, ~2× host RAM)
+
+The reference thinker (MAXTOK ladder needed 768 — r1's think span ran 1313 chars). Third
+plain-transformer in the matrix: every fork classification prediction reproduced.
+
+**Recommended recipe (single-shot / cold sessions):**
+
+```bash
+bmoe-cli -m Qwen3-30B-A3B-Q4_K_M.gguf \
+  --moe-stream --cache-mb auto --io-threads 4 --overlap --dense-weights anon
+```
+
+**Add for served / multi-turn sessions:** warmup replay. `--auto-echo` is a verified
+no-op on this template (it renders history reasoning natively — reuse engages from the
+first follow-up without echoing anything back), and `--rs-seq` is not applicable: as a
+plain transformer, divergence turns are free partial chops without snapshots (c4 reused
+22 tokens with rs-seq OFF; c5 ≡ c4, the snapshot pool simply unused).
+
