+## Fits-RAM models — the stack is off; the fork's session layer is the value
+
+One barely-fitting edge (9.9 GB), one comfortable hybrid (5.0 GB), one comfortable plain
+MoE (4.0 GB). Zero to near-zero faults in the baseline — the streaming engine has no
+thrash to eliminate and pays its overhead instead (−6% to −31%). The fork's session
+layer is the whole show, and the plain transformers get its warmup for free.
+
+### Ling-mini-2.0 (`bailingmoe2` plain MoE, 9.9 GB, ~barely fits host RAM)
+
+The matrix's sharpest fits-RAM result: the streaming stack's own 7.5 GiB cache pushed a
+9.9 GB model INTO swap — the cache became the memory pressure. Non-thinking model.
+
+**Recommended recipe (single-shot / cold sessions):**
+
+```bash
+bmoe-cli -m Ling-mini-2.0-Q4_K_M.gguf --ubatch 512
+```
+
+**Add for served / multi-turn sessions:** warmup replay — reuse engages from the first
+follow-up with no echo (native reuse, non-thinking template). The aider agent session is
+the highlight: cross-edit-turn reuse **87.5%** (turn B: 576 prompt tokens, 504 reused,
+prefill 20.7 s), divergence anchored at the re-sent changed-file snapshot — batch edits;
+non-edit follow-ups ride the cache.
+
+<details>
+<summary><strong>Per-flag table (provenance marked) — click to expand</strong></summary>
+
+| Flag | Provenance | Measured on this model | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| streaming stack (a→b) | **bmoe-main** | **−31%** (12.59 → 8.63 tok/s), prefill 5.6× slower, faults 0.86 → **19.27**/tok — the 7.5 GiB expert cache plus anon dense copy pushed the model into swap: the cache became the memory pressure | **Off** — the model-plus-cache sum exceeded RAM |
+| `--ubatch 512` | **mainline** | protocol default | **On** (protocol) |
+| warmup replay (bridge) | **fork** | T1 prefill 7.9 → **0.80 s (~10×)** | **On** for served use |
+| `--auto-echo` (bridge) | **fork** | verified no-op (c3 ≈ c2, plus warm-cache decode gains); native reuse from the first follow-up (c1 T2 27/34) | **Off** (redundant on a non-thinking template) |
+| `--rs-seq 64` | **fork** (seam PR #29085) | not applicable — c4 divergence a free partial chop (27/34) with rs-seq OFF; c5 ≡ c4 (pool unused) | **Off** |
+| `--ngram` | **mainline** (ngram-mod) | not measured on this model | workload-dependent |
+
+</details>
+
+**Totals (two metrics).** (1) bmoe vs llama: **negative** (−31%) — the one regime where
+the engine actively loses, and the reason the streaming stack is not a default. (2) fork
+vs bmoe-main: warmup ~10×; native reuse from the first follow-up; and the aider
+edit-turn proof (87.5% cross-edit reuse) is the fork's headline agentic number — the
+session layer paying exactly where agent workloads diverge.
+
